      "title": "[SI] joint commemorative coin",
      "link": "https://www.ecb.europa.eu/euro/coins/comm/html/index.en.html",
      "summary": "joint commemorative coin Commemorative coins are identical to the general circulation €2 coin in terms of dimensions and in terms of physical properties. They have a common European side, and a national side with a motif marking an event of wider international significance or of major significance to Slovenia. They are issued only once a year, except when euro area countries opt to issue a joint commemorative coin . Commemorative coins are legal tender in all euro area countries.",
